        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6b30345e-5a3d-5548-80a3-08c48f79f844",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Lotus 49, Cosworth DFV, Arrows A2\n- People: Colin Chapman, Maurice Philippe, Riccardo Patrese, Jochen Mass\n- Companies: Ford, Lotus Cars\n- Works: 9 Days in Summer\n- Topics: Formula One\n\nFacts:\n- Anthony Colin Bruce Chapman was born on 19 May 1928 and later became an influential English automotive design engineer, inventor, builder, and the founder of Lotus Cars.\n- The Lotus 49 was a Formula One racing car designed by Colin Chapman and Maurice Philippe for the 1967 Formula One season.\n- In 1967, the Lotus 49 took part in nine Formula One races.\n- Ford made the promotional documentary film 9 Days in Summer about the development of the Ford-funded Cosworth DFV and the Lotus 49.\n- The title 9 Days in Summer refers to the nine Formula One races in which the Lotus 49 competed in 1967, and those races are extensively featured in the film.\n- Anthony Colin Bruce Chapman died on 16 December 1982.\n- The Arrows A2 was powered by a Cosworth DFV V8 engine and was driven by Riccardo Patrese and Jochen Mass.\n- The Arrows A2 was relatively unsuccessful, with its best finish being sixth place on two occasions.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cb6910a2-092f-5b82-811f-9279035891b1",
        "text": "Page: Lotus 49. Sentence: The Lotus 49 was a Formula One racing car designed by Colin Chapman and Maurice Philippe for the 1967 F1 season.\nPage: Colin Chapman. Sentence: Anthony Colin Bruce Chapman CBE (19 May 1928 – 16 December 1982) was an influential English design engineer, inventor, and builder in the automotive industry, and founder of Lotus Cars.\nPage: 9 Days in Summer. Sentence: 9 Days in Summer is a promotional documentary film made by Ford that tells the story of the development of the Ford-funded Cosworth DFV and Lotus 49, the title coming from the nine Formula One races the car took part in 1967, which are also extensively featured in the film.\nPage: Arrows A2. Sentence: Powered by a Cosworth DFV V8 engine and driven by Riccardo Patrese and Jochen Mass, it was relatively unsuccessful with its best finish being sixth on two occasions.",
